Vikram and Betal: The Proud Scholar (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100123

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a scholar who was very proud of his knowledge,” said Betal. “He believed he knew everything.”

One day, he came to the king’s court and said, “No one is wiser than me.”

The king decided to test him.

He asked a simple farmer to come to the court.

The king told the farmer to ask the scholar a question.

The farmer asked, “Sir, if you know everything, can you tell me what I am thinking right now?”

The scholar was confused and could not answer.

The farmer smiled and said, “I was thinking that even a wise man cannot know everything.”

The court laughed.

The scholar felt ashamed and understood his mistake.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what did the scholar learn?”

Vikram replied, “He learned that no one knows everything.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

No one knows everything; always stay humble.
